    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0244" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23725: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Nogales</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dyer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nogales, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-26T11:00:00-07:23"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1920—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:44
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Southern Pacific will take on railroad [<hi rendition="#italic">freight?</hi>] at
                    noon. Telegram was received today saying that Consul General de Negri at New
                    York after protesting to President Carranza about his course toward Sonora
                    without avail tendered his resignation and has proffered his services to
                    Sonora.</p>
                <p>Governor de la Huerta has accepted appointment, under Plan of Agua Prieta<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d147-f1"/> just issued by Calles, as chief executive, civil
                    and military, for States allying themselves with Sonora.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dyer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
